{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal model using scvi_n200 RNA encoding, ResNet50 image encoding, avgpool aggregation, and concatenation fusion with multiprofile settings. The validation accuracy of 0.6315 suggests multiprofile and aggregation may improve performance compared to singleprofile baselines, though the exact contribution of each factor remains uncertain without direct comparisons. The higher accuracy relative to previous singleprofile setups (e.g., 0.5362 in experiment 004) indicates potential benefits from multiprofile and aggregation, but the role of RNA encoder selection or fusion method is not isolated in this configuration."
}

